      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Flexible endoscopes have both a wide range of movement and a wide field of view and are thus widely used for endoscopic third ventriculostomy and biopsy. However, tumor resection using flexible endoscopes has scarcely been reported, likely owing to their single port, which has a diameter of 1.2-2.0 mm. Furthermore, flexible endoscopes do not allow some of the basic neurosurgical manipulations, especially sharp dissection with counter tension. Additionally, the position of the forceps and coagulators is fixed within the endoscope. Here we report a new technique of dissection used on two tumors located in the posterior third ventricle. Technical aspects and potential advantages of this approach are also briefly discussed."
      },
